Interpretation: if (2) >> (1), the profiler's floor is event overhead,
and the small-kernel rows in the report are inflated by that constant.
If (3) << (1), graph replay already hides most of the dispatch cost.
The number that governs Phase 4x is (7): deleting an isolated norm node
saves its isolated cost, deleting one behind a busy stream saves (7).
The number that governs the MEGAKERNEL is (8): if a busy node's overhead
is far below an empty node's, the toll is already overlapped and a
persistent kernel buys little.  (8b) tests the same thing via the
profiler's own instrument and says whether that instrument is lying.
